  dialogueSoundChanges: []
  dialogueScrollSpeeds: []
  defaultScrollSpeed: 30
  defaultLines:
  - You come back from a tough day of adventuring to find a letter waiting for you.
  - You open the letter.
  - '"Hey, kid, I know it''s been a while!"'
  - '"I should probably ask if you''re doing well like any other father would,"'
  - '"But I''ll cut to the chase; If you''re reading this that means I''ve passed
    away." '
  - '"Don''t be alarmed! we both knew this kind of thing could happen with you going
    on your adventures." '
  - '"You always been the free spirit sort, but if you what put down roots for any
    reason." '
  - '"Just know I''ve left my old resturant waiting for you in good ol'' Kriesen." '
  - '"It''ll be a bit of a fixer upper, but I''m sure you''ll do great!" '
  - '"I mean you remember all the recipes I taught you, right?" '
  - '"Now you might be wondering how I sent you this letter with me being dead and
    all?" '
  - '"Hah! Guess your old man still had some tricks that you didn''t know about!" '
  - '"Take care, kid!" '
  - '"Love, Dad" '
  - 'You close the letter, wondering what to do. '
  - '. . . . Maybe a change of pace would be nice? '
  - "After many days of travel, you arrive at the town of Kriesen and at your father\u2019s
    restaurant as his letter instructed. "
  - 'You push open the door, hearing a crack of aged wood as you move it.  '
  - 'You cough instinctively at the abundance of dust. '
  - "Well, there\u2019s nothing more to it; you head to the pantry to, ready to start
    cooking, only to find "
  - ' .... Nothing but cobwebs and dust. Oh, and your father''s old recipe book. '
  - 'Guess you''ll have to gather the ingredients yourself. '
  dayDialogues: []
  loadSceneAfterDialogue: 1
  nextSceneName: Room1
  autoCreateUiAtRuntime: 1
  defaultSpeakerName: Narrator
  soundname: uiClick
